[120.418457, "o", "tNode, all its neighbors have opened = BY_START. Then end-side expansion of startNode checks its neighbors. First neighbor checked: if neighbor.opened === BY_START → YES! So it returns biBacktrace(neighbor, startNode)!\\n\\nSo biBacktrace(neighbor, startNode) where neighbor has parent = startNode (set in start-side expansion), and startNode has parent = ... nothing (it's the start node). Wait:\\n- In start-side expansion: `neighbor.parent = node` where node = startNode\\n- biBacktrace(node, neighbor) where node is from start-side (startNode) and neighbor is from end-side expansion\\n\\nWait, I need to re-read the code more carefully.\\n\\nIn the end-side expansion loop, `node` is what was popped from endOpenList (which is startNode = endNode). So biBacktrace(neighbor, startNode) traces neighbor's parent chain back to startNode, then concatenates with startNode's parent chain—but startNode has no parent since it's the root, so I need to check the actual biBacktrace implementation to see how it handles this.\",\"sign"]
